# The Kiwi Network app catalog.
# Register it once per machine:
#   kiwi catalog add https://github.com/derlocke-ng/kiwi-catalog.git
#
# ONE line per app, even when the app installs both a root service and a
# desktop component. The app's own kiwi.manifest declares which scopes it
# needs (SCOPES=user system), so this file does not repeat it.
#
# Optional per-entry overrides:
#   branch=<name>    track a branch instead of release tags
#   ref=<tag>        pin to an exact version
#   scope=<user|system>
#                    install only that half on this machine, even if the app
#                    declares both. A filter, not a declaration.
#
# Apps follow their latest version tag; repos without tags follow HEAD.

https://github.com/derlocke-ng/kiwi-updater.git
https://github.com/derlocke-ng/kiwi-killswitch.git
https://github.com/derlocke-ng/ensconce.git
https://github.com/derlocke-ng/kiwi-cli-tools-desktop.git
# kiwi-proxy before the apps that use it: kiwi-fox's identities, kiwi-pentesting's
# tools and the provider modules below all exit through its gateways.
https://github.com/derlocke-ng/kiwi-proxy.git
https://github.com/derlocke-ng/kiwi-fox.git
https://github.com/derlocke-ng/kiwi-server.git
https://github.com/derlocke-ng/syncman.git

# Provider modules — each gives kiwi-proxy a SOCKS5/VPN exit, for kiwi-fox and
# everything else that uses it. Installed into kiwi-proxy's modules directory;
# kiwi-proxy manages their lifecycle. They depend on kiwi-proxy, which kiwi
# installs first (releases before 0.2.0 went to kiwi-fox, and depend on it).
https://github.com/derlocke-ng/kiwi-plugin-tor.git
https://github.com/derlocke-ng/kiwi-plugin-vpn.git
https://github.com/derlocke-ng/kiwi-plugin-9proxy.git
https://github.com/derlocke-ng/kiwi-plugin-myst.git
